ABOUTME: quiche patch applied by build-libquiche.sh: raise the receive-window maximums of a live
ABOUTME: connection and read its connection window (upstreamable as is; the diff starts below).

Raise the receive-window maximums of a live connection

Config::set_max_connection_window() and Config::set_max_stream_window()
bound receive-window autotuning, but only for connections created
afterwards. An application that accounts for receive memory must then
either pin the windows (no autotuning) or commit to the largest window
for every connection up front.

Add Connection::set_max_connection_window() and
Connection::set_max_stream_window(), the live connection's equivalents
(the latter applies to existing and future streams; neither lowers a
maximum below the current window), and Connection::connection_window(),
which returns the current connection-level window, so an application can
grant more window to a connection once it can afford to. Exposed through
the FFI as quiche_conn_set_max_connection_window(),
quiche_conn_set_max_stream_window() and quiche_conn_connection_window().

